[center]
[size=6][b][color=#e6b85c]M.A.R.A.S[/color][/b][/size]
[size=4][b]Marriage, Affairs, Relationships, Ancestry & Society[/b][/size]
[size=3][i]Marry anyone. Build a family dynasty. Run households across Skyrim — or watch marriages implode in scandal and alimony.[/i][/size]
[/center]

[line]

[quote]
[b][color=#e6b85c]Safe-For-Work Core | Zero Plugin Slots Used (ESL-Flagged) | In-Game Dashboard (Alt + B) | Two Tailored Ways to Play[/color][/b]
M.A.R.A.S is completely [b]SFW out of the box[/b], takes zero full slots in your load order, and adapts cleanly to your setup! Play [b]Classic RPG Mode[/b] (structured dialogue menus, social-standing proposal checks, persuasion rolls, and dice-roll world simulation) OR pair it with [b]SkyrimNet AI Mode[/b] (where proposal menus step aside for natural voice/text roleplay, and winning someone over comes down to your shared history and silver tongue). M.A.R.A.S also hooks seamlessly into [b]Fertility Mode Reloaded / Beeing Female NG[/b] and [b]OStim / SexLab[/b] whenever you choose to install them!
[/quote]

[heading]WHY M.A.R.A.S?[/heading]

Ever looked at a Jarl, a grumpy blacksmith, a chaotic necromancer, or that one shopkeeper who keeps overcharging you and thought: [i]"They would make a great addition to my household"[/i]?

In vanilla Skyrim, marriage and family life feel like an afterthought. You put on a necklace, chop firewood once, sit through a two-minute ceremony, adopt at most two kids, and leave your spouse staring at a wall in Breezehome for the next four hundred hours while they bake pies and hand you 100 gold.

[b][color=#e6b85c]M.A.R.A.S turns Skyrim into a living, breathing simulation of marriage, households, ancestry, affairs, and social drama.[/color][/b]

To set expectations clearly: [b]M.A.R.A.S is not a scripted dating-sim about buying bouquets or going on candlelit dinner dates.[/b] Think of it like [i]Crusader Kings[/i] or [i]The Sims[/i] social and family systems dropped straight into Skyrim. Both [b]you[/b] and [b]NPCs across the province[/b] can partner up, marry, manage households and wealth, raise and train heirs, keep secrets, cheat behind closed doors, fight over child custody, and suffer financially ruinous divorces.

[size=4][b][color=#e6b85c]Play Any Kind of Story You Want[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]The Devoted Soulmate:[/b] Stay faithful to a single spouse to unlock a [b]doubled 2x Devotion Bonus[/b] on their household perks, legally share their home (yes, even a palace!), adopt as many orphans as you want, and build a peaceful home together.
[*][b]The Dynasty Builder:[/b] Earn Mara's divine blessing for [b]Polygamy[/b], rank a household of spouses across multiple estates, run specialized home shops, and send your children off to [b]22 guilds, colleges, temples, and shrines[/b] until they return as full-grown adult adventurers and followers.
[*][b]The Soap-Opera Antihero:[/b] Juggle casual side lovers, negotiate open relationships, hide secret affairs, survive bedroom walk-ins, dodge furious alimony bills, and watch secret paternity scandals blow up across Whiterun.
[*][b]The Province-Wide Social Architect:[/b] Press [b]Alt + B[/b] anytime to open the modern in-game [b]M.A.R.A.S Dashboard[/b] — pair up or split any two NPCs in Skyrim, follow the province gossip feed, or let the background matchmaker evolve Skyrim's society automatically.
[/list]

[line]

[heading]WHAT'S INSIDE: COMPLETE FEATURE LIST[/heading]

[size=4][b][color=#e6b85c]1. Modern In-Game Dashboard (Alt + B) — Goodbye Laggy Menus![/color][/b][/size]
Forget scrolling through dozens of slow, clunky MCM pages. Press [b]Alt + B[/b] anytime during gameplay to open a sleek, responsive window right over your game:
[list]
[*][b]Your Household at a Glance:[/b] Check every partner's affection mood, manage spouse hierarchy ranks, assign homes, track active buffs, and look after your children and pets in one place.
[*][b]Province-Wide Gossip & Directory:[/b] Search every adult NPC in Skyrim, inspect their family tree and relationship history, read the live [b]Activity Feed[/b] of new couples and breakups, or teleport straight to a lost spouse or child.
[*][b]Intrigue Mode (Spoiler-Free Secrets):[/b] Enabled by default! Undiscovered affairs, unannounced pregnancies, and secret biological fathers stay masked in the menu so you are never spoiled on twists your character hasn't uncovered in-game yet — unless you click [b]Secrets[/b] to peek behind the curtain.
[*][b]Built for Comfort & Translations:[/b] Pause the game automatically on open, expand to Full Screen, scale text and menus from [b]75% to 150%[/b] for 4K TVs or Steam Deck, and switch languages on the fly without restarting Skyrim.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#e6b85c]2. Marry Anyone & Pick Your Commitment Level (No Forced Steps!)[/color][/b][/size]
If they are an adult human, elf, or beastfolk in Skyrim, they are fair game — with zero clutter added to NPC dialogue until you initiate:
[list]
[*][b]No Forced Ladder (Lover -> Dating -> Engaged Is NOT Required):[/b] Want marriage, household perks, and a family? [b]Propose marriage right away[/b] straight from [b]Candidate[/b] — you do not need to be Lovers or Date first! Prefer an exclusive relationship without getting married? Choose [b]Dating[/b]. Want zero commitment or exclusivity? Keep them as a casual [b]Lover[/b]. Relationships can also end in [b]Ex-Lover[/b], [b]Ex-Dating[/b], [b]Jilted[/b] (left at the altar!), or [b]Divorced[/b].
[*][b]Two Ways Proposals Are Decided:[/b] In [b]Classic Mode (without SkyrimNet)[/b], dialogue proposals use M.A.R.A.S's [b]Marriage Chance & Social Standing[/b] checks — weighing Affection alongside Speech, Gold, Owned Homes, Heroic Fame, and Guild Reputation against their Social Class. In [b]SkyrimNet AI Mode[/b], those marriage-chance stat rolls [b]do not apply[/b] — there are no stat gates to brute-force; you win someone over purely through your shared history and your talent for convincing them in conversation!
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#e6b85c]3. Household Life, 14 Spouse Buffs, 9 Home Shops & Sharing Their Home[/color][/b][/size]
Every NPC in Skyrim is classified by [b]Social Class[/b], [b]Skill Type[/b], and emotional [b]Temperament[/b] ([i]Romantic, Jealous, Proud, Humble,[/i] or [i]Independent[/i]) — making every marriage feel genuinely different:
[list]
[*][b]14 Unique Spouse Buffs:[/b] Married spouses grant [b]8 Always-On Household Buffs[/b] based on their Social Class (Carry Weight, Skill XP, Magic Resist, Sneak Attack Damage, Stamina Regen, Speech skill, and better buying or selling prices) plus [b]6 Combat Buffs[/b] when traveling with you as a follower (Melee/Ranged Damage, Magicka Regen, Stealth, Armor Defense, and faster Dragon Shouts).
[*][b]Dynamic Affection (0-100) & Moods:[/b] Earn trust and loyalty through daily check-ins, gifts suited to their class, sleeping under the same roof, adventuring together, or spending quality time with your kids. Happy spouses boost your buffs by [b]+25%[/b]; neglected spouses grow [i]Troubled[/i] or [i]Estranged[/i] and shut off your perks!
[*][b]9 Specialized Home Shops & Passive Gold:[/b] Spouses living in your homes earn [b]100 gold/day[/b] (up to 500 saved up), cook homemade meals, and open a shop matching their skills — [i]Blacksmith, Spell Merchant, Apothecary, Fletcher, Jeweler, Tailor, Hunter, Innkeeper,[/i] or [i]General Trader[/i].
[*][b]Move Into THEIR Home (Yes, Even Palaces!):[/b] Happy spouses ([b]50+ Affection[/b]) can legally share their personal home with you — giving you keys, bed access, and permission to live and take items there without trespassing!
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#e6b85c]4. Faithful Monogamy vs. Polygamy & Spouse Hierarchy[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Monogamy Devotion Bonus (2x Power):[/b] Prefer a single lifelong partner? Staying married to one spouse automatically [b]doubles[/b] their permanent household buff!
[*][b]Player Polygamy & Household Ranks:[/b] Unlock multiple marriages through a short Shrine of Mara quest ([i]"The Flame Divides Not"[/i]) or a single settings toggle. Rank your spouses from [b]Lead Spouse (1st)[/b] down to [b]4th+[/b] — just have generous gifts ready if you ever demote a [i]Proud[/i] spouse!
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#e6b85c]5. Ancestry, Unlimited Adoptions, 22 Training Academies & Adult Offspring[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Unlimited Adoptions & Pets:[/b] Forget vanilla Skyrim's 2-kid cap! Adopt as many orphans as you want — or assign orphans to [b]NPC married couples[/b] so every orphan in Skyrim gets a home! Every child can own their own [b]Pet Dog[/b] and [b]Wild Critter[/b] (with a one-click ban button if you hate Frostbite Spiders). If both parents of a town child die, the child safely moves to Honorhall Orphanage.
[*][b]Cradle to Adult Follower (Optional Fertility Integration):[/b] With [b]Fertility Mode Reloaded[/b] or [b]Beeing Female NG[/b], raise biological babies (including twins and triplets!) from [b]Expecting -> Infant -> Young Child -> Academy Training -> Grown Adult Adventurer[/b]!
[*][b]22 Training Schools, Guilds, Shrines & Werewolf Packs:[/b] Send children to train at the [i]College of Winterhold, Jorrvaskr, Thieves Guild, Dark Brotherhood, Bards College, Dawnguard, Sky Haven Temple, Imperial Legion, Stormcloaks, House Telvanni, 4 Daedric Shrines,[/i] or [i]2 Werewolf Packs[/i] (unlocked when a child inherits [b]Werewolf Beastblood[/b] from a werewolf parent!). Parents in the same faction even earn tuition discounts.
[*][b]Independent Adult Offspring:[/b] Graduated children enter Skyrim as full-grown adults who inherit their parents' hair, eyes, skin tone, and height, receive starting gold from their guardians, wear gear and cast spells from their academy, travel between inns and family homes on their own, and can join you anytime as loyal followers!
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#e6b85c]6. Affairs, Partner Agency, Paternity Secrets & Costly Divorces[/color][/b][/size]
Your partners aren't lifeless mannequins waiting at home — they have agency, loyalty, and breaking points of their own:
[list]
[*][b]Open Relationships & Two-Stage Affairs:[/b] Negotiate an open relationship ([i]Independent[/i] partners love it; [i]Jealous[/i] partners despise it) — or risk temptation when a closed partner is neglected or sees you cheating first. Affairs start in a [b]Talking Stage[/b] (secret letters and lingering talks) before escalating into a [b]Physical Affair[/b] with someone from their actual town, guild, or household.
[*][b]Home-Arrival Surprises & Tavern Notes:[/b] Come home to a partner waiting to confront or confess to you, walk in on a secret rendezvous red-handed, or find a handwritten note on the table leading you straight to the local tavern!
[*][b]Hidden Affair Pregnancies & Paternity Scandals:[/b] An affair pregnancy stays quiet early on until the mother reveals it or her 2nd-trimester belly shows. If a baby clearly doesn't resemble the presumed father, suspicions skyrocket — leading to confrontations, customizable [b]Divorce Custody[/b], and the true biological father potentially stepping in to claim his child!
[*][b]Ultimatums, Alimony & Inheritance:[/b] Let a spouse's affection fall below 25 and you get [b]3 days[/b] ([i]"Marriage: The Last Word"[/i]) to salvage the marriage before they divorce you and serve a [b]Divorce Settlement[/b] scaled to your gold, houses, horses, quests, and cleared dungeons (refuse to pay, and it goes onto your Hold Bounty!). If a spouse dies, a courier brings a mourning letter and inheritance — [i]unless you were the one who killed them[/i].
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#e6b85c]7. A Living Society: Autonomous NPC Couples & Tavern Gossip[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Automatic World Matchmaking (Both Modes):[/b] Single NPCs across Skyrim pair up, date, marry, break up, move in together, and even carry on secret affairs behind the scenes via customizable dice-roll simulation or the SkyrimNet AI Game Master (while your own partners stay protected under your Partner Agency settings). Track every twist in the Dashboard's [b]Activity Feed[/b]!
[*][b]Ambient Town & Tavern Scenes (Both Modes):[/b] Hear nearby NPC couples chatting, arguing, or confronting each other about lovers, dating, open relationships, or secret affairs as you walk through cities, inns, shops, and temples! Built-in dialogue scenes play with or without SkyrimNet — and with SkyrimNet installed, lines are voiced via TTS alongside live AI conversations.
[/list]

[line]

[heading]TWO WAYS TO PLAY: CLASSIC MODE VS. SKYRIMNET AI[/heading]

M.A.R.A.S automatically reshapes its dialogues and mechanics depending on whether [b]SkyrimNet[/b] is installed — hiding redundant menu dialogues when AI roleplay takes over, while keeping AI-only actions exclusive to SkyrimNet players. [i](You can even toggle "Simulate No SkyrimNet" in Settings anytime to test or compare Classic Mode!)[/i]

[size=4][b][color=#7cc4fa]Classic RPG Mode (Without SkyrimNet)[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Full (M) Dialogue Menus:[/b] Everything is accessible right through crisp Skyrim dialogue menus — register Candidates, give gifts, propose Lover, Dating, or Marriage, question faithfulness, confess affairs, negotiate open relationships, break up, and resolve the 3-day [i]"Marriage: The Last Word"[/i] crisis.
[*][b]Social-Standing & Speech Mechanics:[/b] Proposal acceptance uses M.A.R.A.S's [b]Marriage Chance & Prestige Calculator[/b] (Affection, Speech, gold, owned homes, fame, and guild alignment vs. their Social Class), while affair confrontations and marriage ultimatums rely on Affection-weighted rolls and [b]Speech / Persuasion / Intimidation[/b] checks.
[*][b]Weighted Dice-Roll Simulation & Ambient Scenes:[/b] Background NPC-to-NPC matchmaking, partner temptation, and paternity secret discovery run automatically via fast, customizable dice-roll probabilities — while built-in ambient NPC couple and affair scenes play out right in towns and taverns.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#e6b85c]SkyrimNet AI Mode (With SkyrimNet Installed)[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Clean, Uncluttered Menus:[/b] Redundant [b](M)[/b] proposal, breakup, open-relationship, and affair-confrontation dialogue topics automatically hide so static menu prompts never interrupt AI roleplay — while practical household topics (moving homes, sharing their house, shop gold, meals, spouse ranks, and giving gifts) stay right in dialogue and the Dashboard!
[*][b]Sway Them With Words, Not Stat Rolls:[/b] You (or NPCs!) propose Lover, Dating, or Engagement, argue, confess or expose affairs, reveal hidden pregnancies or paternity, or demand a divorce naturally through [b]18 live AI actions[/b] exclusive to SkyrimNet mode. [b]Marriage-chance stat formulas do not apply to SkyrimNet proposals[/b] — success depends purely on your shared history, their personality, and how persuasively you make your case!
[*][b]Real-Time Voice Acting (TTS) & "Decline (Explain)":[/b] Voices unvoiced M.A.R.A.S dialogue lines aloud in real time [i](you can even use SkyrimNet purely for TTS voice acting with AI chat turned off)[/i], and adds a [b]Decline (Explain)[/b] button to relationship pop-ups so you can turn down an NPC's proposal in character.
[*][b]Strict "No Psychic Spouses" & Living Memories:[/b] Enforces strict secret isolation so partners never magically know affairs or paternity secrets they haven't witnessed or been told, voices ambient couple scenes while letting NPCs spark live AI conversations nearby, powers AI Game Master matchmaking, and carries [b]first-person memories[/b] all the way from childhood into adulthood!
[/list]

[line]

[heading]HOW TO PLAY: PLAYER QUICK-START GUIDE[/heading]

New to M.A.R.A.S? You don't need to memorize a textbook — everything adapts smoothly to whether you are playing Classic Mode or SkyrimNet AI Mode, backed up anytime by the [b]Alt + B[/b] Dashboard!

[b]Click "Show" below for the Instant "How Do I...?" Cheat Sheet:[/b]
[spoiler]
[b][color=#e6b85c]Open the M.A.R.A.S Dashboard:[/color][/b] Press [b]Alt + B[/b] during gameplay (rebindable in [i]Settings -> General[/i]).

[b][color=#e6b85c]Start Tracking Any Adult NPC:[/color][/b] Talk to them and pick [b]"(M) Ever think we could be something more?"[/b] (in SkyrimNet mode, you can also speak naturally right away).

[b][color=#e6b85c]Give Gifts (Both Modes) or Propose / Break Up (Classic Mode):[/color][/b] Choose [b]"(M) May I have a word with you?"[/b] — in Classic Mode this holds your Lover, Dating, Marriage, Open Relationship, and Breakup menus; in SkyrimNet Mode those menus stay hidden so you handle proposals, breakups, and confessions directly in voice/text chat!

[b][color=#e6b85c]Manage Homes, Spouse Ranks, Meals & Shop Gold (Both Modes):[/color][/b] Talk to your spouse and choose [b]"(M) Can we talk about our life together?"[/b] (or manage everything in [i]My Household[/i] inside the Dashboard).

[b][color=#e6b85c]Move Into Your Spouse's Personal Home:[/color][/b] Reach [b]50+ Affection[/b], talk to them about where you are living, and ask [b]"Is your home open to me as well?"[/b] Then step inside their home to unlock full access!

[b][color=#e6b85c]Let a Housed Jarl or Shopkeeper Keep Their Day Job:[/color][/b] Open their profile in the Dashboard ([b]Alt + B[/b]) and uncheck [b]Stay at Home[/b] (or tell them in dialogue they can head back during the day).

[b][color=#e6b85c]Unlock Multiple Marriages (Polygamy):[/color][/b] Be married + have at least 1 absorbed Dragon Soul + [b]sleep in any bed[/b] to start [i]"The Flame Divides Not"[/i] and pray at a Shrine of Mara — OR toggle [b]Enable Polygamy[/b] in [i]Settings -> General[/i].

[b][color=#e6b85c]Send Kids Out of the Room:[/color][/b] Happens [b]automatically[/b] when an OStim/SexLab scene starts! You can also ask your child in dialogue to go play outside, or click [b]Send Kids[/b] in the top bar of the Dashboard.

[b][color=#e6b85c]Spawn Biological Kids or Send Them to Training:[/color][/b] Always use your child's profile inside the [b]M.A.R.A.S Dashboard (Alt + B -> My Household -> Children)[/b] — never the old Fertility Mode / Beeing Female MCM buttons!
[/spoiler]

[size=4][b][color=#7cc4fa]Step 1: Pick Your Path — Casual, Dating, or Straight to Marriage[/color][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Walk up to any adult NPC in Skyrim and pick [b]"(M) Ever think we could be something more?"[/b] This registers them as a Candidate with [b]zero neglect decay[/b] — take all the time you want!
[*]You do [b]not[/b] need to climb a ladder from Lover -> Dating -> Engaged. Go straight to whichever arrangement fits your story: propose [b]Marriage[/b] right away if you want a spouse and household, stay at [b]Dating[/b] if you want exclusivity without marriage, or keep things as zero-commitment [b]Lovers[/b].
[*]Select [b]"(M) May I have a word with you?"[/b] anytime to give [b]Gifts[/b] (match the gift's value to their Social Class — a modest gem thrills a miner, while a noble expects fine jewelry!). Daily affection gains have sensible daily caps so you can't dump 300 iron daggers on someone in five minutes to cheese their affection.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#7cc4fa]Step 2: Winning Their Hand — Classic Stats vs. SkyrimNet Roleplay[/color][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*][b]Without SkyrimNet (Classic Mode):[/b] Open [b]"(M) May I have a word with you?"[/b] and choose [b]"Will you marry me?"[/b] (or propose Lover / Dating). Their answer depends on M.A.R.A.S's proposal chance check — weighing Affection, Speech, carried gold, owned homes, quest fame, and guild standing against their Social Class. If they turn you down, wait 24 in-game hours to build standing or adjust proposal difficulty in [b]Settings[/b].
[*][b]With SkyrimNet AI:[/b] Static proposal menus hide automatically so they never break immersion — simply make your case in voice or text chat! Marriage-chance formulas [b]do not block you here[/b]: it comes down to your shared history, their personality, and how well you persuade them to choose you.
[*]Your first marriage starts the classic Temple of Mara ceremony in Riften. For repeat weddings (or right away via [b]Settings -> General[/b]), you can [b]skip the ceremony[/b] and become married on the spot! Stand them up at the altar, however, and they become [b]Jilted[/b] until you apologize and win back their trust.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#7cc4fa]Step 3: Household Management, Home Shops & Protecting Quest NPCs[/color][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Move a spouse into any owned vanilla or modded Player House via dialogue or the [b]Assigned Residence[/b] dropdown on their Dashboard profile.
[*][b][color=#e6b85c]Golden Rule for Jarls, Merchants & Quest NPCs:[/color][/b] Moving someone into your house tells them to stay around home. If you married a town blacksmith, Jarl, or quest giver who needs to be at their job during the day, simply uncheck [b]Stay at Home[/b] on their Dashboard profile! They will still count toward your household while keeping their normal daily routine.
[*]Keep a housed spouse above [b]50 Affection[/b] to shop at their specialized home stall and collect [b]100 gold per day[/b]!
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#7cc4fa]Step 4: Keeping Partners Happy (Or Surviving the Fallout)[/color][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*][b]The Grace Period:[/b] By default, you can travel away from home for [b]2 in-game days[/b] before partners start losing affection (adjustable from [b]1 to 14 days[/b], or slide affection decay down to [b]0.0[/b] in [i]Settings -> General[/i] for a relaxed, penalty-free playthrough!).
[*][b]The Adventurer's Advantage:[/b] Bring a spouse along as an active [b]Follower[/b]! Traveling together prevents loneliness completely, grants [b]+6 Affection every day[/b], and activates their [b]Follower Combat Buff[/b].
[*][b]Avoiding Alimony:[/b] If a spouse drops below [b]25 Affection (Estranged)[/b], [i]"Marriage: The Last Word"[/i] begins. Visit them within [b]3 days[/b] to salvage the marriage — pass a Persuasion/Intimidation check or give gifts in [b]Classic Mode[/b], or talk things out genuinely in roleplay in [b]SkyrimNet Mode[/b] — otherwise prepare your coin purse for a divorce settlement!
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#7cc4fa]Step 5: Raising Heirs, Academy Training & Playing Matchmaker[/color][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*][b]Adopt Anyone, Anywhere:[/b] Adopt orphans through dialogue, or open [b]Dashboard -> Matchmaking -> Child Adoption[/b] to bring kids into your household (or assign orphans to happy NPC couples!).
[*][b]From Cradle to Adult Follower:[/b] Using [i]Fertility Mode Reloaded[/i] or [i]Beeing Female NG[/i]? When your baby grows into a young child, a naming window pops up with custom and lore-friendly racial names. Open their Dashboard profile to click [b]Spawn Child[/b] so they live at home, [b]Send to Training[/b] to enroll them in one of 22 academies, and [b]Spawn Adult[/b] upon graduation to meet your grown-up adventurer son or daughter!
[*][b]Shape Skyrim's Society:[/b] Open [b]Dashboard -> Matchmaking[/b] anytime to pair up or split any two NPCs manually, or let background matchmaking evolve town families while you adventure.
[/list]

[line]

[heading]REQUIREMENTS, INSTALLATION & MIGRATION[/heading]

[size=4][b][color=#8fd694]Required Mods[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://skse.silverlock.org/]SKSE64[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444]Address Library for SKSE Plugins[/url]
[*][url=https://github.com/Severause/MagelightUI]Magelight UI[/url] — [i]Powers the in-game Alt + B Dashboard and pop-up windows (replaces Prisma UI from older releases!)[/i]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/12604]SkyUI[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/13048]PapyrusUtil SE[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/22854]powerofthree's Papyrus Extender[/url]
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#7cc4fa]Optional Mods (Supported Out of the Box!)[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b][url=https://github.com/MinLL/SkyrimNet-GamePlugin]SkyrimNet[/url]:[/b] Unlocks SkyrimNet AI Mode — real-time TTS voice acting (including ambient couple scenes), 18 conversational AI actions where words and history sway NPCs instead of stat rolls, autonomous AI matchmaking, and persistent memories.
[*][b]Fertility Mode Reloaded (v1.0.7+ REQUIRED)[/b] or [b]Beeing Female NG (v3.6.4+ REQUIRED):[/b] Adds biological pregnancy, childbirth, child naming, 22 training academies, grown adult follower children, and secret paternity drama. [i](Older versions of these two mods are missing essential birth events — please make sure yours is up to date!)[/i]
[*][b]OStim Standalone[/b] or [b]SexLab:[/b] Automatically awards partner affection for intimate scenes, triggers cheating walk-in confrontations if caught, and sends awake children out of the room automatically.
[*][b]Optional Translations Pack:[/b] Installing a non-English language pack from Optional Files? Grab [b]Dynamic String Distributor (DSD)[/b] so translated dialogue and quest text load cleanly without touching the main plugin!
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#e6b85c]Upgrading From Pre-v2 (0.x / 1.x) or Earlier 2.x Releases[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Cleanly Replace (Do Not Merge!) Old Mod Files:[/b] In Mod Organizer 2 or Vortex, uninstall your old version or choose [b]Replace[/b] — [i]never Merge[/i] — over pre-v2 (0.x / 1.x) installations so retired legacy scripts and old loose SkyrimNet prompt/action files are removed cleanly in favor of the [i]tetherball88.maras[/i] SkyrimNet bundle. [i](If you use SkyrimNet, make sure your SkyrimNet plugin is up to date as well.)[/i]
[*][b]Install Magelight UI (Goodbye MCM & Prisma UI):[/b] Pre-v2 used SkyUI MCM and 2.0-2.5 used Prisma UI. Install [b]Magelight UI[/b] to power the [b]Alt + B Dashboard[/b] and pop-up windows. On pre-v2 saves where the old MCM was already registered, SkyUI MCM simply keeps a small stub menu with an [b]Open M.A.R.A.S Dashboard[/b] button while all settings now live inside [b]Alt + B[/b].
[*][b]Automatic Pre-v2 Save Upgrade:[/b] Load your pre-v2 save and give M.A.R.A.S a few seconds to finish initializing — your existing spouses, engagements, divorces, jilted partners, affection scores, custom trait overrides, Spouse Hierarchy ranks, assigned Player Houses, shared spouse homes, NPC home markers, and old MCM settings ([i]Skip Wedding[/i], confirmation toggles, etc.) upgrade automatically, guarded by built-in [b]Save Upgrade Protection[/b].
[*][b]First-Load Import Checklists:[/b] Existing Hearthfire adopted children, active Fertility Mode / Beeing Female pregnancies and children, and pre-set follower ties open in an interactive [b]Import Checklist[/b] so you choose exactly what to bring into v2+ tracking.
[/list]

[b]Click "Show" below for New Game / Mid-Playthrough Installation & Compatibility Tips:[/b]
[spoiler]
[b][color=#8fd694]Installing on a New Game or Mid-Playthrough:[/color][/b]
Install with Mod Organizer 2 or Vortex and enable [b]TT_MARAS.esp[/b] (it is ESL-flagged and takes zero full plugin slots). Installing mid-playthrough on an existing save is supported! On first load, M.A.R.A.S automatically imports vanilla NPC couples and shows you a clean [b]Import Checklist[/b] for any existing player marriages, modded follower ties, adopted kids, or active pregnancies so you choose what to bring in.

[b][color=#7cc4fa]Compatibility & Load Order:[/color][/b]
M.A.R.A.S does [b]not[/b] edit vanilla NPC records or overwrite vanilla quests, making it compatible out of the box with NPC appearance overhauls, city overhauls, custom followers, multi-follower frameworks, and modded player homes! Just remember: Skyrim still runs its original quests, so if you marry Vittoria Vici, the Dark Brotherhood still has a contract on her!
[/spoiler]

